WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
Two glasses of blue sports
drink stand side by side.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.000
Same shade.

3
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.560
Same depth of blue.

4
00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.620
To the eye, they match.

5
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.960
Yet one of them holds
more dye than the other.

6
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.060
White light contains
every visible wavelength.

7
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.360
Could a beam of it settle the question?

8
00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:20.740
How could light tell which
glass holds more dye?

9
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.240
In this mission, you'll meet
the instrument: a lamp,

10
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.980
a sample in a small clear cell
called a cuvette, and a detector.

11
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.800
Then you'll make a set of standard
solutions and plot a calibration graph.

12
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: find out how a beam of light
can tell which drink holds more dye.